    "https://www.coe.edu/alumni/c3-creativity-careers-community": {
      "title": "C3: Creativity, Careers, Community",
      "description": "Support C3: Creativity, Careers, Community | Coe College Skip to main content Search This Site Plan a Visit Apply Request Info Toggle navigation Admission Expand Menu Become a Kohawk Learn about majors, apply for admission, discover campus life, connect with Coe and much more! Schedule A Visit First-Year Students International Students Transfer Students Online Students Visit Request Information Parents School Counselors Financial Aid & Scholarships Majors & Areas of Study Meet Your Counselor Why Coe? Submit Your Enrollment Fee Destination: Cedar Rapids Iowa Ready – Regent Price Match Aviation Studies & Flight Operations Student Checklist Virtual Tour Engineering & Physics Visit Day Academics Expand Menu Think Like a Kohawk With more than 60 areas of study that cover a range of fields, you're sure to find your interests. Explore Academics at Coe Majors & Areas of Study - On Campus Coe Online The Coe Difference - Centers and Programs Academic Resources Stewart Memorial Library Student Life Expand Menu Live Like a Kohawk Get ready for lasting memories, new friendships, and the countless fun activities. Explore Student Life Clubs & Organizations Athletics Religious & Spiritual Life Health & Wellness Residence Life Title IX Community Standards & Expectations Student Life Resources Contact Student Life Why Coe Expand Menu Explore Like a Kohawk Coe College is a selective, private, nationally recognized four-year coeducational liberal arts institution providing superior educational experiences for students since 1851. Learn About Coe Events News & Features Discover Coe Faculty/Staff Directory Consumer Information Parents & Visitors Visitor Information Kohawk Stories The Perfect College Town Legends of Coe Women of Coe Progress with Purpose Athletics Expand Menu Play like a Kohawk Coe College sports are fun, lively, competitive and awesome. Find news, schedules, and other information about Coe Sports here. Go to kohawkathletics.com Sports Master Schedule Recruit Me News Archive Hall of Fame Campus Map Staff Directory Alumni Expand Menu Once a Kohawk, Always a Kohawk Life after Coe is full of opportunity and promise. Join alumni in clubs, activities and life. Connect today! Coe College Alumni Support Coe Alumni & Friends Engagement Publications Make a Gift C3: Creativity, Careers, Community Advancement Services FAQs Careers Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Visitors Request Info Search This Site Coe Alumni C3: Creativity, Careers, Community C3: Creativity, Careers, Community C3 expands Coe's alumni connections to assist students with planning and carrying out projects, forming professional networks and putting their Coe experiences to work in the wider world. Volunteer opportunities Please use the \"Volunteer Form\" button on the left in order to let us know where your interests lie. Alumni speaker Are you interested in sharing your career story? Do you, or does your company, have a specialty you think would help our students in their career journey? Join our repository of Coe Alumni willing to speak with current students about any career-related topics. (Either in the classroom, with student organizations, or at events.) We will provide faculty and student groups this repository once a year, in the fall. We will contact alumni as needed. Competition mentors and judges Do you have an entrepreneurial spirit and proven entrepreneurial success? Sign up and be part of the annual Kohawk Startup innovation event where students pitch ideas, form teams, work with professional mentors on customer discovery and research, then \"sell\" their business plan to a panel of judges! Participants will be designated as either mentors or judges as needed based on student participation. INT100 speaker Are you willing to participate in a class? Share your expertise? Join a repository of Coe Alumni willing to speak at C3's Professionalism and Self-Presentation class. This 0.2 credit class is presented by C3 and meets each Spring semester. Topics can include: LinkedIn and how to use, Resumes, Interviewing tips and skills, Networking - how to network and why it's important, Workplace expectations and Boundary setting. Speakers are not guaranteed and will be contacted based on class participation and needs. LinkedIn Careers Community speaker As a Coe Alumnus we welcome you to join Coe's LinkedIn Careers Community. Each LinkedIn's Careers Community is free and is designated to facilitate communication between students, alumni and community members about varying career paths . Please select from the links below and submit your request. Once approved, you will be able to network and engage with your chosen community(ies). Coe College Science Research Careers Community Coe College Data and Technology Careers Community Coe College Business and Entrepreneurism Careers Community Coe College Arts, Communications, Media, and Entertainment Careers Community Coe College Legal, Law Enforcement, and Public Service Coe College International Affairs, Government, and Public Policy Coe College Natural Resources, Agriscience, and Environment Career Community Coe College Social Sciences, Counseling, and Education Coe College Health and Wellness Careers Community Post your job on Handshake Coe College uses the online job board, Handshake . Handshake is being used by over 900 colleges nationally, including other Corridor-area colleges and universities. What this means is that you can broadcast your recruiting needs to a larger audience. Use the link to create an employer profile and once approved, you may post your company's jobs and internships. Alumni recruiting policy Want to hire a Kohawk? Use your Handshake profile to post your job. C3 will communicate with students and faculty through Handshake using targeted outreach to certain majors, school year, and/or year of graduation. Check out the C3 & Alumni Engagement Recruiting Request guide to hiring a Kohawk. Do you need career advice? Click here for resources to get started or email o-career@coe.edu to speak with a career specialist. Who we are Joe Demarest Director of C3 I can help you with: Networking Internships Career mentoring Kris Jasper Career Specialist I can help you with: Networking Interview Job search Ellen Teller Career Specialist I can help you with: Networking Job search Internships To contact us or find a complete directory of the Advancement staff, click here . Questions? For more information, visit our FAQ page . In This Section Support Coe Ways to give Annual Fund Because of you Fundraising Events 50th Class Reunion gift Annual golf outing and fundraiser Crowdfunding 1851 Next 1851 Society Planned Giving Athletic Day of Giving State of the College Thankful Thursday Day of Giving Alumni & Friends Engagement Alumni Events Homecoming Volunteer Opportunities Kohawk Event Kits Alumni Council Pat Steele, President Charles Cotton, Vice President Constance Schlitter Losch, Secretary Lauren DuBay Gilbertson, Past President Sally Brause Carla Brooks Jay Caughren Matt Clark Tara Crosby Amy Duru Kirk Ergang Dominic Fails Nick Ludwig Jenny McArdle Darcy Moulin Troy Orwan Verlynn Schmalle Bill Waldie Alumni Benefits & Resources Alumni Awards Alumni Award of Merit Distinguished Service Award Young Alum Award Founders' Medal Stay Updated Coe Traditions 175 Years of Coe 2026 Oral History Project Publications Make a Gift C3: Creativity, Careers, Community Alumni C3 Resources Advancement Services FAQs volunteer form Apply & Enroll Plan a Visit Calendar of Events Give Resources Directory Maps & Directions Consumer Information Webcasts Privacy Policy Quick Links Bookstore The Kohawk Shop Campus Calendar Majors & Areas of Study Library My Coe (my.coe.edu) Moodle Request Information Facebook icon Instagram icon TikTok icon Twitter icon LinkedIn icon Youtube icon 1220 First Avenue NE, Cedar Rapids, IA 52402 | 877.Call.Coe or 319.399.8500 | admission@coe.edu © 2026 Coe College | All rights reserved. Web Application by Informatics, Inc"
